{"availability":"available","full":"nakanoasaservice/uuid58","name":"uuid58","description":"A tiny, zero-dependency library for generating and converting UUIDs to Base58-encoded strings.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":47,"forks":1,"created":"2025-04-28T16:57:12Z","updated":"2026-07-23T02:08:06Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://nakanoasaservice.github.io/uuid58-playground/","topics":["base58","uuid"],"demo":"https://nakanoasaservice.github.io/uuid58-playground/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:40.789Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:40.789Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:40.789Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:43:40.789Z","stars":47,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A tiny, zero-dependency library for generating and converting UUIDs to Base58-encoded strings (using Bitcoin-style alphabet). Perfect for creating shorter, URL-safe identifiers while maintaining the uniqueness of UUIDs.","Standard UUIDs are 36 characters long (including hyphens), which can be cumbersome in URLs or when space is limited. Base58 encoding reduces this to a fixed 22 characters while maintaining uniqueness and using only URL-safe characters. The Base58 alphabet used in this library is the same as Bitcoin's, which excludes similar-looking characters (0, O, I, l) to prevent visual ambiguity and confusion."],"features":["🚀 Generate short, URL-safe identifiers (fixed 22 characters)","🔄 Bidirectional conversion between UUID and Base58","🪶 Zero dependencies","💪 Type-safe with TypeScript","🔒 Uses native crypto.getRandomValues() for secure UUID generation"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nakanoasaservice/uuid58/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5af25916235fd01b9eb58cfac400b781f76ce9a5e644d5943f9662728f4195bf","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:40.885Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:40.885Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A ti